 "一世": "جِيل, نَسْل (A single step or stage in the succession of natural descent; a rank or degree in) / جِيل (The average amount of time needed for children to grow up and have children of t)  [generation] / عُمْر (The amount of time that some being has been alive, or that some thing has been i) / سِنّ (Any particular stage of life.)  [the age] / أَوَّل, أُولَى (Coming right after the zeroth in things that use zero-based numbering.) / أَوَّلاً (Before anything else; firstly.) / أَوَّل (The person or thing in the first position.)  [the first (e.g. Elizabeth I)]\nمثال: １６０３年、ジェームズ一世が政権の座についたとき、フットボールは再び許可されたのです。\n→ In 1603, when King James I came into power, football was allowed again. / [issei ; first-generation Japanese (or Korean, etc.)]",
 "一世紀": "قَرْن, عَصْر (A period of one hundred consecutive years; often specifically a numbered period )  [century]\nمثال: １世紀は１００年です。\n→ A century is one hundred years.",
