 "世間ばなし": "كَلَام خَفِيف, مُحَادَثَة خَفِيفَة (Idle conversation, typically regarding innocuous or unimportant subjects, usuall)  [small talk]\nمثال: 世間話をしなくてもいいからね。\n→ You don't have to chat with them.",
 "世間一般": "مُجْتَمَع, جَمَاعَة (A long-standing group of people sharing cultural aspects such as language, dress) / جَمْعِيَّة (A group of people who meet from time to time to engage in a common interest; an ) / اِجْتِمَاعِيَّة (The people of one’s country or community taken as a whole.)  [society]\nمثال: 世間一般のホテルなみにいえば良い昼食会だった。\n→ It was a good luncheon, as hotels go.",
 "世間並": "عَادِيّ, مَأْلُوف (Being part of the natural order of things; normal, customary, routine.)  [ordinary (esp. life or behavior)]\nمثال: 我々も世間なみのことをしなくちゃ。\n→ We had better do what other people do.",
 "世間並み": "عَادِيّ, مَأْلُوف (Being part of the natural order of things; normal, customary, routine.)  [ordinary (esp. life or behavior)]\nمثال: 我々も世間なみのことをしなくちゃ。\n→ We had better do what other people do.",
 "世間体": "ظُهُور (The act of appearing or coming into sight; the act of becoming visible to the ey) / مَظْهَر (A thing seen; a phenomenon; an apparition.) / مَظْهَر, شَكْل (The way something looks; personal presence) / شَكْل (Apparent likeness; the way which something or someone appears to others.)  [appearance (in the eyes of society)]\nمثال: 彼は世間体を気にしない。\n→ He has no regard to appearance.",
 "世間様": "عالم (The Universe.) / عَالَم, دُنْيَا (The Earth, especially in a geopolitical or cultural context, or as the physical ) / عَالَم, دُنْيَا (An individual or group perspective or social setting.)  [world]\noft. sarcastic",
 "世間的": "عَلَنِيّ, عَامّ (Pertaining to the people as a whole, as opposed to a group of people; concerning) / عُمُومِيّ (Officially representing the community; carried out or funded by the government o) / عَامَّة, جُمْهُور (Chiefly preceded by the: members of the community or the people in general, rega)  [public (attention, recognition, etc.)]",
